Figure 3 illustrates the transient inflammatory response and cellular uptake of Nano-11 at the injection site, key to its adjuvant activity. Panel a demonstrates the kinetics of various inflammatory cells, showing a peak in recruitment around day 2, predominantly Mac-2+ macrophages, which then declines, indicating a transient response. Panel b, through confocal microscopy, visually confirms the uptake of labeled Nano-11 (red) by MHCII+ antigen-presenting cells, Ly6C+ monocytes, and Mac-2+ macrophages from 6 hours to day 7 post-injection. This highlights Nano-11's ability to localize and deliver antigen to critical immune cells, promoting efficient antigen processing and presentation for an enhanced immune response, while maintaining a favorable safety profile due to the transient nature of the inflammation.